systemtap
gcc
# Name the DANOS headers explicitly rather than the linux-headers-amd64
# metapackage. Both DANOS and Debian ship a package with that exact name, and
# apt picks by version: once trixie moved to 6.12.105-1 it outranked our
# 6.12.101-1vyatta1, so the metapackage pulled in Debian's headers and, through
# their dependency, Debian's linux-image as well. The image then carried two
# kernels and live-build made the newer one -- Debian's -- the default boot
# entry, which is not the kernel the dataplane is built against.
linux-headers-6.12.0-trunk-vyatta-amd64
# linux-compiler-gcc-10-x86: our 6.12 kernel was built with gcc-10, but trixie's
# repos don't ship gcc-10 at all, so this compiler-tracking package for systemtap
# has no installable candidate. Non-essential (debug/tracing tooling only).
#linux-compiler-gcc-10-x86
#linux-image-4.19.0-trunk-vyatta-amd64-dbg
